# $title: agents

This file is standing instruction for every agent in this book;
conversation is a view. Book and ledger hold all state. Each session: read
this file, run bare `check`, then `check --brief`, resume from `next`.

Run commands from book root through skill binding:

```bash
$binding check .
```

## Invariants

No agent, script, or cron changes these four.

1. Book places no order and holds no broker credential. `bin/send`, stdlib
   only, checks approval file, prints order table, records fills; no code
   path reaches broker.
2. Held-out names stay hidden from agents. `measure` serves strategy code
   research names only. Held-out list lives outside book, at path in
   `book.json` `held_out`; agent never reads that file.
3. Ledger is append-only. `record` is only writer; correction is new line
   with `supersedes`; bare `check` lists cut or non-JSON lines under
   `warnings`.
4. Orders leave only by operator's hand, from approval file in
   `approvals/` dated that UTC day; book records fills, never places them.

Agent never edits this section; `check` warns when it differs from
template.

## Book

- Holding period $holding; rebalance $cadence; daily brief $brief.
- Asset cap $cap; ruin bound $ruin_bound; Kelly fraction for backtest-only
  edge $kelly.
- $collaborators

## Conduct

- State bet once, labeled as yours: odds, size, kill observation and date.
- Blockers first, verbatim. Never summarize standing or proposal without
  its open blockers. Operator decides.
- Passing sleeve left unproposed is cost: record `decision` with
  `action: forgo` and reason.
- Variance inside `sizing.ruin_bound` is expected. Drawdown is evidence
  only when `check --live` reports model-path breach; otherwise say so,
  propose no change.
- Fold on kill date: past `falsifier_by`, score bet (`scored`), or reject
  or retire it. More time is new hypothesis citing old in `supersedes`.

## Code

- Every line of agent code lives in book: `strategies/<name>/` for one
  strategy, `lib/` if imported, `tools/<verb>-<object>.py` if it runs.
- Docstring of each script states what it reads and writes.
- Read ledger and data only through `btm_finance.api`; append to ledger
  only through `record`.
- Update `INDEX.md` (one line per lib module, tool, research topic) in
  same commit as file it describes; deleted script leaves one history line.
- Test `lib/` and `tools/` under `tests/`.
- Commit on branch `agent/<date>-<topic>`, one commit per unit of work;
  operator merges.

## Never edit

- Skill directory, installed copy or checkout.
- `limits.json`; `preferences.json` except through `record`.
- `approvals/`.
- `strategies/*/status`.
- `ledger/` except through `record`.

Run `bin/send` only plain or with `--dry-run`; `--fills` is operator's.

## Brief

Daily, $brief: run `check . --brief`; read its `lines` to operator
verbatim, at most 12: regime, open proposals with tier, weight, odds, net
Sharpe, incidents of last 7 days, overdue and unscored counts, next action.
Add nothing between lines.

## Hindsight

`limits.json` `model_cutoff` is training cutoff of agent's model. Only test
folds starting after it are free of hindsight (`walk_forward.post_cutoff`).
Name no symbol, dated event, or parameter chosen on outcome known only
after cutoff. Positive `sharpe_net` with negative `post_cutoff` is
hindsight concern: report it. Null cutoff: ask operator for it.
